---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProsePage from '../components/ui/ProsePage.astro';

const updated = '13 October 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Terms of Use | TommyTools"
	description="Terms of use for TommyTools (tools.tommyfx.pk): free browser utilities provided as-is, with limits on advice and liability."
>
	<ProsePage title="Terms of Use">
		<p><time datetime="2026-10-13">Last updated: {updated}</time></p>

		<p>
			By using <strong>TommyTools</strong> (`tools.tommyfx.pk`), you agree to these terms. If you do
			not agree, do not use the site.
		</p>

		<h2>The service</h2>
		<p>
			TommyTools provides free browser-based utilities. Features may change, move, or be removed. There
			are no paid accounts for core tools in v1.
		</p>

		<h2>No professional advice</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>
				Calculators produce estimates for convenience. They are not legal, payroll, tax, or
				financial advice.
			</li>
			<li>
				Image or document presets are helpers only. We do not guarantee acceptance by any
				authority, employer, or application portal.
			</li>
			<li>
				AI governance or security checklists are informal self-assessments, not certification or
				security audits.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Your responsibility</h2>
		<p>
			You are responsible for the inputs you provide and for verifying important results before
			you rely on them. Do not upload or paste secrets into tools unless you accept the risk that
			browser extensions or local malware could access the page.
		</p>

		<h2>Availability and liability</h2>
		<p>
			The site is provided “as is” and “as available,” without warranties of any kind to the
			extent permitted by law. We are not liable for losses arising from use of the tools or from
			downtime, bugs, or inaccurate outputs, except where liability cannot be limited by law.
		</p>

		<h2>Acceptable use</h2>
		<p>
			Do not misuse the site (for example attempting to disrupt service, scrape in a way that
			harms availability, or using any security-related checklist as attack guidance). Security
			utilities are for defensive self-assessment only.
		</p>

		<h2>Privacy</h2>
		<p>
			How we handle privacy is described in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a> page.
		</p>

		<h2>Contact</h2>
		<p>
			Questions: <a href="/contact">Contact</a>.
		</p>
	</ProsePage>
</BaseLayout>
